/-!
Properties of `Compiler/src/ssair/domtree.jl` (dominator and post-dominator trees, their
dynamic updates and queries) and of the CFG edits in `Compiler/src/ssair/ir.jl` that feed them.
The model is `JuliaLean/Compiler/src/ssair/domtree.lean` and `.../ssair/ir.lean`.

Topic files under `domtree/`: `Spec` (dominance by definition), `Checks` (the checks and the
family `smallCFGs` of small CFGs), `Props` (the statements), `Bounded*` (exhaustive kernel
evaluation over `smallCFGs`), `Basic` and `General` (general properties of the small functions,
the CFG edits, `_dominates` and `nearest_common_dominator`) and `Refuted`.
-/

namespace JuliaLean.Proofs.Compiler.src.ssair.domtree

open JuliaLean.Registry

private def dt : String := "Compiler/src/ssair/domtree.jl"
private def ir : String := "Compiler/src/ssair/ir.jl"

/-- The bound shared by the `-small` entries. -/
private def small : String :=
  "the 639 CFGs of smallCFGs: every CFG with 1 or 2 blocks (successor lists without a repeated block, in any order; the virtual predecessor 0 on block 1, and also on block 2), every 3-block CFG with increasing successor lists (virtual predecessor on block 1), the 48 other 3-block CFGs compute_basic_blocks can give (block 1 branching [3, 2], with and without block 3 as a catch block), and 27 CFGs of 4 to 9 blocks in compute_basic_blocks shapes chosen because they reach the update branch of snca_compress! and its recursion (forward and in post-dominance, 6 of each kind), five- and three-level kill_edge! recursion, and the 9-block delete counterexample; with self loops, irreducible loops, back edges into block 1, catch blocks, unreachable blocks and cycles"

